    "body": "@domfarolino regarding referrer policy for srcdoc iframes, I would be in favour of not treating it in a special way. I like to keep a consistent behaviour where policies are inherited at document creation time, but then each document has its separate own policies. Or are there any strong arguments for making the policies of a srcdoc iframe a \"reference\" to the parent's policies?\r\n\r\nAlso, notice that the \"reference\" behaviour makes implementing srcdoc iframes out-of-process more problematic (that's something that no vendor implements at the moment AFAIK but I guess it is something we might want to have - for example for sandboxed srcdoc iframes). I understand that is not a problem of the html spec, but we might want to keep that in mind nevertheless.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/809999922/reactions",
